  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 602.21 Ground cover",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 602.21 “Ground cover” means any herbaceous plant or any woody seedling or shrub generally less than 3 feet in height. The term does not include lawns, landscaped areas, gardens, invasive species as listed by the department of agriculture, markets, and food in accordance with RSA 430:53, III, exotic aquatic species listed pursuant to Env-Wq 1303, imported organic or stone mulches, or other artificial materials.\n\nSource. #12806, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt600.html"
